  8 years ago](https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/enabling-data-driven-experiences-luis-caballero)
  
  [iframe](https://www.linkedin.com/embed/feed/update/urn:li:share:7434749288955473921)
  
  [We expanded live translation for headphones on iOS](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Fproducts-and-platforms%2Fproducts%2Ftranslate%2Flive-translate-with-headphones%2F&urlhash=Poan&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block), and to more countries. Google Translate’s [Live translate with headphones](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Fproducts-and-platforms%2Fproducts%2Fsearch%2Fgemini-capabilities-translation-upgrades%2F&urlhash=ay2t&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block) has arrived on iOS, and we've expanded the capability for both iOS and Android users in even more places. Live translate helps you instantly understand and connect with the world around you right through any pair of headphones in over 70 languages.
  
  [iframe](https://www.linkedin.com/embed/feed/update/urn:li:ugcPost:7443144976324030466?collapsed=1)
  
  [We announced new tools and partnerships to support your health at The Check Up 2026](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Finnovation-and-ai%2Ftechnology%2Fhealth%2Fgoogle-health-check-up-2026%2F&urlhash=8RXC&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block).At our annual health event, we shared how AI can help spark medical breakthroughs and bring quality healthcare to everyone, everywhere. We’re providing [$10 million in funding to help organizations](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Finnovation-and-ai%2Ftechnology%2Fhealth%2Fgoogle-check-up-health-ai-updates-2026%2F&urlhash=YJ6o&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block) reimagine clinician education in the AI era, and exploring new partnerships with rural health leaders focused on education, care delivery and research. Plus, [Fitbit is making its health tracking even better](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Fproducts-and-platforms%2Fdevices%2Ffitbit%2Ffitbit-personal-health-coach-updates-2026%2F&urlhash=KdbM&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block) with  expansions to the personal health coach in Public Preview that will give you more personalized advice about your sleep and overall health, the ability to connect your medical records to the Fitbit app, plus [new features for cycle health, mental wellbeing and nutrition and water logging](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Fproducts-and-platforms%2Fdevices%2Ffitbit%2Ffitbit-personal-health-coach-new-features%2F&urlhash=UVZZ&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block).
  
  [We introduced Lyria 3 Pro for enhanced music generation](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Finnovation-and-ai%2Ftechnology%2Fai%2Flyria-3-pro%2F&urlhash=3aLi&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block). This update brings our most advanced music model to more products, enabling you to generate tracks up to three minutes long with granular control over specific elements like intros, verses, and bridges. Additionally, Lyria and Lyria 3 are now available in [public preview for developers](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Finnovation-and-ai%2Ftechnology%2Fdevelopers-tools%2Flyria-3-developers%2F&urlhash=fgTq&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block) through the Gemini API and [Google AI Studio](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Faistudio%2Egoogle%2Ecom%2Fnew_music&urlhash=tF6d&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block), expanding the tools available for creative AI expression.
  
  [iframe](https://www.linkedin.com/embeds/publishingEmbed.html?articleId=8906270343318818457)
  
  We released [Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Finnovation-and-ai%2Fmodels-and-research%2Fgemini-models%2Fgemini-3-1-flash-lite%2F&urlhash=eEaX&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block) and [Gemini 3.1 Flash Live](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Finnovation-and-ai%2Fmodels-and-research%2Fgemini-models%2Fgemini-3-1-flash-live%2F&urlhash=CCoo&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block). Flash-Lite is our fastest, most budget friendly model yet. It’s built to quickly handle heavy workloads without compromising quality. Its low latency makes it an ideal solution for building responsive, real-time experiences while maintaining significant cost efficiency for large-scale deployments. Plus, we released Gemini 3.1 Flash Live, our best audio model to date. It’s fast and sharp enough to feel like a real conversation, and it’s already live in more than 200 countries via Search Live and Gemini Live. By cutting down the lag and boosting precision, we’re helping developers and businesses build reliable tools for their customers.
  
  [We launched an upgraded vibe coding experience in Google AI Studio](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fblog%2Egoogle%2Finnovation-and-ai%2Ftechnology%2Fdevelopers-tools%2Ffull-stack-vibe-coding-google-ai-studio%2F&urlhash=ZqK7&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block). Building an app should feel as easy as talking about one. Google AI Studio now lets you turn prompts into production-ready apps, by using the new Google Antigravity coding agent. You can use Build mode to build multiplayer experiences, add databases, connect to real-world services, and more. The new AI agent has a much deeper understanding of your entire project, which means faster iterations and more precise code edits, and it securely stores your API keys and lets you pick up exactly where you left off. Go to [Google AI Studio](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=http%3A%2F%2Faistudio%2Egoogle%2Ecom%2Fapps&urlhash=H2DX&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block) to start building.
  
  [We looked back at 10 years of AlphaGo’s impact](https://www.linkedin.com/redir/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdeepmind%2Egoogle%2Fblog%2F10-years-of-alphago%2F&urlhash=zI_x&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block). A decade after its historic win over a world champion of an incredibly complex game, we looked back at how AlphaGo proved AI could navigate the world’s most complex challenges and better understand the vast complexities of the physical world. This milestone served as the foundational spark for AlphaFold solving the 50-year-old “protein folding” problem. By finally mapping these 3D structures, AlphaFold opened the door to better understanding diseases and a new age of AI-driven scientific breakthroughs.
  
